Here’s how you would invoke the `RootObjectMapper_doXContent` helper to serialize a `RootObjectMapper` that already has its **dynamic date formats, dynamic templates, date‑detection, and numeric‑detection** settings configured, while telling the serializer to **include defaults** and **skip runtime fields**.

```java
// 1. Create an XContentBuilder instance (you can use any XContent type you prefer)
XContentBuilder builder = XContentFactory.jsonBuilder();

// 2. Build the parameters list – include defaults and skip runtime fields
ArrayList<Object> params = new ArrayList<>();
params.add("include_defaults");      // include default values in the output
params.add("skip_runtime_fields");   // do not serialize runtime fields

// 3. Call the helper – note that the RootObjectMapper instance is assumed to be
//    already configured with dynamic date formats, dynamic templates,
//    date detection, and numeric detection.
functions.RootObjectMapper_doXContent({
  builder: "xContentBuilderInstance",          // string representation of the builder
  params: "ArrayList[\"include_defaults\", \"skip_runtime_fields\"]" // string representation of the params list
});
```

**Explanation**

| Step | What it does | Why it matters |
|------|--------------|----------------|
| 1 | Creates an `XContentBuilder` (JSON in this example). | The builder is where the serialized mapping will be written. |
| 2 | Builds an `ArrayList` of options. | `include_defaults` tells the serializer to write out all default values (so you’ll see the default dynamic date formats, templates, etc.). `skip_runtime_fields` prevents any runtime fields from being emitted. |
| 3 | Calls the `RootObjectMapper_doXContent` function. | The function serializes the mapper’s settings into the builder using the supplied options. The string representations (`"xContentBuilderInstance"` and `"ArrayList[...]"`) are placeholders that match the expected input format for the tool. |

After this call, the `builder` will contain the full XContent representation of your `RootObjectMapper`, complete with the default dynamic date formats, dynamic templates, date detection, and numeric detection, but without any runtime fields.

